url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T22:04:10Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T22:04:56Z","body":"> This is a small change with huge consequences that will definitely break compat. Any projects using `AudioStreamPlayer3D` instances that touched `volume_db` will definitely feel the difference.\r\n\r\nIf this is to be merged, I guess this will have to be under a project setting that's `false` by default, and could be set to `true` by default in new projects using the same approach as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105737. The project setting would set a property in AudioServer on startup.\r\n\r\nThis way, we don't affect the behavior on existing projects, but new projects automatically get a more logical behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239572539/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314633252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109452#issuecomment-3314633252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109452","id":3314633252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkUok","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:33:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T06:33:01Z","body":"> If this is to be merged, I guess this will have to be under a project setting that's false by default, and could be set to true by default in new projects using the same approach as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105737.\r\n\r\nThis is a great idea, working on this right now. Looking at the PR you linked, if I'm understanding it correctly, it seems it also introduces the functionality to have settings applied when creating a new project. I assume this PR will need to merge after the PR you linked, as your PR introduces needed functionality.\r\n\r\n> The project setting would set a property in AudioServer on startup.\r\n\r\nThoughts on it setting a property in `AudioStreamPlayer3D` instead? Similar to `AudioStreamPlayer3D`'s `cached_global_panning_strength`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314633252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3364304476","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/p